WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.977
A bad agent can repeat the same failure.

00:00:02.977 --> 00:00:06.152
Imagine the first search query is refund.

00:00:06.152 --> 00:00:08.987
The retriever returns weak evidence.

00:00:08.987 --> 00:00:14.082
The rewrite step produces exactly the same word, refund.

00:00:14.082 --> 00:00:21.403
The next search returns the same chunks, the grader rejects them again, and the process repeats.

00:00:21.853 --> 00:00:24.010
That is not meaningful reflection.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.875
Nothing changed. A good controller should detect no progress.

00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:33.560
If the query did not change, change strategy or stop.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:40.565
If the same document I D's keep returning, try another source, filter, or retriever.

00:00:40.565 --> 00:00:45.053
If useful evidence is always rejected, inspect the grader.

00:00:45.603 --> 00:00:51.155
Every retry should create information gain or change the search strategy.

00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:55.110
Otherwise, another loop is simply extra cost.
